## Summary
Brazil passed the General Data Protection Law (LGPD) in 2018, which came into effect in February 2020. This article compares the LGPD to the EU's GDPR, highlighting key differences and similarities in data protection regulations.

## Key Points
- LGPD was enacted in 2018 and became effective in February 2020.
- It is Brazil's equivalent to the GDPR, focusing on data privacy and protection.
- The article examines how LGPD differs from GDPR in terms of implementation and scope.
- Information is sourced from GDPR.eu, a platform dedicated to GDPR compliance and related laws.


